        # Actually in CPython, validate=True means "if True, non-alpha characters in the data will raise an error."
        # Whitespace is still skipped? Let me check: from docs, "If validate is False (the default), characters that are neither in the normal base-64 alphabet nor the alternative alphabet are discarded prior to the padding check. If it is True, these non-alphabet characters in the input result in a binascii.Error."
        # So with validate=True, whitespace IS an error.
